  16:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // Reference implementation of the DebugLog() function that's required for a
  17:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // platform to support the TensorFlow Lite for Microcontrollers library. This is
  18:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // the only function that's absolutely required to be available on a target
  19:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // device, since it's used for communicating test results back to the host so
  20:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // that we can verify the implementation is working correctly.
  21:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // This function should support standard C/C++ stdio style formatting
  22:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // operations. It's designed to be as easy as possible to supply an
  23:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // implementation though. On platforms that have a POSIX stack or C library, it
  24:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // can be written as a single call to `vfprintf(stderr, format, args)` to output
  25:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // a string to the error stream of the console, but if there's no OS or C
  26:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // library available, there's almost always an equivalent way to write out a
  27:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // string to some serial interface that can be used instead. To add an
  28:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // equivalent function for your own platform, create your own implementation
  29:lib/tflite-micro/tensorflow/lite/micro/debug_log.cc **** // file, and place it in a subfolder with named after the OS you're targeting.
